1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,910
Twelve boys and their coach,

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:05,253
trapped four kilometers inside a flooded mountain.

3
00:00:05,253 --> 00:00:07,810
No food. Barely any air.

4
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,907
And some of them couldn't even swim.

5
00:00:09,907 --> 00:00:11,507
So how do you get thirteen people

6
00:00:11,507 --> 00:00:12,787
out of a cave that's full of

7
00:00:12,787 --> 00:00:13,167
water?

8
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:18,411
June 2018

9
00:00:18,411 --> 00:00:20,771
Twelve boys from a youth football team head

10
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:22,771
into a cave in northern Thailand,

11
00:00:22,771 --> 00:00:24,402
with their young coach

12
00:00:24,402 --> 00:00:24,402
While they're deep inside...

13
00:00:26,441 --> 00:00:27,994
it starts to rain

14
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:27,994
The water rises fast

15
00:00:29,901 --> 00:00:31,960
And it cuts off the only way out

16
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:31,960
Outside,

17
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:34,780
their families gather at the cave entrance,

18
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:35,869
praying

19
00:00:35,819 --> 00:00:35,869
For days,

20
00:00:36,489 --> 00:00:38,489
nobody knows if they're even alive,

21
00:00:38,489 --> 00:00:41,089
somewhere deep inside a flooded mountain

22
00:00:41,216 --> 00:00:41,216
What happened next became one of the most

23
00:00:43,236 --> 00:00:45,316
daring rescues ever attempted

24
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:45,712
This is the true story of the Thai cave

25
00:00:47,692 --> 00:00:48,812
rescue

26
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:54,175
So who were these boys?

27
00:00:54,175 --> 00:00:56,535
They were between eleven and sixteen years old,

28
00:00:56,535 --> 00:00:59,135
members of a team called the Wild Boars

29
00:00:59,398 --> 00:00:59,668
They lived in Mae Sai,

30
00:01:00,968 --> 00:01:02,888
a small town in northern Thailand,

31
00:01:02,888 --> 00:01:05,210
right by the border with Myanmar

32
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:05,210
After football practice,

33
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:09,070
they rode their bikes to the Tham Luang cave

34
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:11,310
with their twenty-five-year-old assistant

35
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:12,430
coach

36
00:01:12,221 --> 00:01:12,491
They'd made the trip before

37
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,933
It was supposed to be a fun little adventure

38
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:17,253
But this wasn't just any cave

39
00:01:19,323 --> 00:01:21,163
It was one of the longest in Thailand,

40
00:01:21,163 --> 00:01:23,163
with tunnels stretching for miles under a

41
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:24,230
mountain

42
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:24,230
About ten kilometers of narrow passages,

43
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:28,490
chambers and tunnels

44
00:01:28,354 --> 00:01:28,624
The plan was to stay for about an hour

45
00:01:31,053 --> 00:01:33,181
They brought almost no food

46
00:01:32,911 --> 00:01:33,181
At the entrance,

47
00:01:33,861 --> 00:01:36,241
a sign warned visitors not to go in during

48
00:01:36,241 --> 00:01:37,241
the rainy season,

49
00:01:37,241 --> 00:01:39,321
from July to November

50
00:01:39,079 --> 00:01:39,349
But the rainy season was about to begin

51
00:01:41,988 --> 00:01:42,408
Nobody knew that this one-hour trip would last

52
00:01:44,708 --> 00:01:46,148
eighteen days

53
00:01:50,233 --> 00:01:51,033
Deep inside,

54
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:53,153
the boys had no idea what was happening

55
00:01:53,153 --> 00:01:53,972
outside

56
00:01:53,972 --> 00:01:56,572
Heavy monsoon rain had started to fall

57
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:56,810
Rainwater soaked down through the mountain,

58
00:01:58,830 --> 00:02:01,430
and poured into the cave from every direction

59
00:02:01,616 --> 00:02:01,886
It flooded the narrow tunnels behind them

60
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:07,250
Some passages filled with water all the way to

61
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:08,465
the ceiling

62
00:02:08,195 --> 00:02:08,465
With the water chasing them,

63
00:02:09,926 --> 00:02:11,605
they moved deeper and deeper,

64
00:02:11,605 --> 00:02:13,614
looking for higher ground

65
00:02:13,344 --> 00:02:13,614
And all they had for light were a few

66
00:02:15,314 --> 00:02:16,434
flashlights

67
00:02:16,422 --> 00:02:16,692
Finally,

68
00:02:17,272 --> 00:02:19,272
they scrambled onto a muddy slope,

69
00:02:19,272 --> 00:02:21,872
about four kilometers from the entrance

70
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:21,912
There was little space,

71
00:02:22,972 --> 00:02:24,251
and little air

72
00:02:24,251 --> 00:02:24,691
But here,

73
00:02:24,691 --> 00:02:25,211
at least,

74
00:02:25,211 --> 00:02:27,107
the water couldn't reach them

75
00:02:26,837 --> 00:02:27,107
Outside,

76
00:02:27,807 --> 00:02:29,647
someone spotted their bikes at the cave

77
00:02:29,647 --> 00:02:30,400
entrance

78
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,392
The search had begun

79
00:02:31,972 --> 00:02:32,392
Parents rushed to the cave,

80
00:02:33,852 --> 00:02:34,732
and stayed there,

81
00:02:34,732 --> 00:02:36,492
day and night

82
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:41,840
Now imagine being in there

83
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,246
Total darkness

84
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,366
Cold

85
00:02:44,266 --> 00:02:44,536
The boys huddled together on the muddy slope to

86
00:02:47,036 --> 00:02:48,373
stay warm

87
00:02:48,103 --> 00:02:48,373
With no food,

88
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:51,433
they drank clean water dripping from the cave

89
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:52,450
walls

90
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:52,450
To save the batteries,

91
00:02:53,670 --> 00:02:55,669
they used their flashlights as little as

92
00:02:55,669 --> 00:02:56,789
possible

93
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:56,800
Their coach had once trained as a monk

94
00:02:59,029 --> 00:03:00,789
So he taught the boys to meditate,

95
00:03:00,789 --> 00:03:03,285
to stay calm and save energy

96
00:03:03,015 --> 00:03:03,285
Breathing slowly and sitting still meant using

97
00:03:05,705 --> 00:03:06,947
less energy...

98
00:03:06,947 --> 00:03:08,498
and less air

99
00:03:08,228 --> 00:03:08,498
They took turns digging at the walls,

100
00:03:10,358 --> 00:03:12,894
hoping to find another way out

101
00:03:12,624 --> 00:03:12,894
They dug a few meters

102
00:03:14,731 --> 00:03:16,741
But the rock was too hard

103
00:03:16,471 --> 00:03:16,741
Days passed

104
00:03:18,130 --> 00:03:20,174
No sign of rescue

105
00:03:19,754 --> 00:03:20,174
What they didn't know was that outside the

106
00:03:22,193 --> 00:03:22,754
mountain,

107
00:03:22,754 --> 00:03:24,993
thousands of people were already looking for

108
00:03:24,993 --> 00:03:26,113
them

109
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:30,033
Outside,

110
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:32,425
Thai Navy divers tried to swim in

111
00:03:32,425 --> 00:03:34,553
But the current was too strong

112
00:03:34,283 --> 00:03:34,553
The Navy set up a base inside the cave,

113
00:03:36,853 --> 00:03:37,853
and kept trying,

114
00:03:37,853 --> 00:03:39,388
day after day

115
00:03:39,118 --> 00:03:39,388
Soon,

116
00:03:39,968 --> 00:03:42,128
experts arrived from all over the world:

117
00:03:42,128 --> 00:03:43,128
cave divers,

118
00:03:43,128 --> 00:03:43,768
soldiers,

119
00:03:43,768 --> 00:03:45,528
engineers and doctors

120
00:03:45,534 --> 00:03:45,804
Teams came from Britain,

121
00:03:47,104 --> 00:03:48,144
the United States,

122
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:48,984
Australia,

123
00:03:48,984 --> 00:03:49,464
China,

124
00:03:49,464 --> 00:03:51,763
Japan and many other countries

125
00:03:51,493 --> 00:03:51,763
Huge pumps worked day and night to pull water

126
00:03:54,383 --> 00:03:55,743
out of the cave

127
00:03:55,473 --> 00:03:55,743
The pumped water was sent into nearby rice

128
00:03:58,163 --> 00:03:58,683
fields,

129
00:03:58,683 --> 00:04:00,763
flooding the farmers' crops

130
00:04:00,650 --> 00:04:00,880
Volunteers searched the jungle on the mountain

131
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:03,780
above,

132
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,846
looking for another way in

133
00:04:05,576 --> 00:04:05,846
Any hole,

134
00:04:06,506 --> 00:04:09,106
any shaft that might lead down into the cave

135
00:04:09,022 --> 00:04:09,292
Thousands of people were now working to find

136
00:04:11,432 --> 00:04:12,800
the boys

137
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:12,800
And volunteers cooked thousands of free meals

138
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:17,660
to keep the rescuers going

139
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:21,613
Then,

140
00:04:21,613 --> 00:04:22,653
on the tenth day,

141
00:04:22,653 --> 00:04:24,993
two British cave divers pushed further than

142
00:04:24,993 --> 00:04:26,352
anyone before

143
00:04:26,082 --> 00:04:26,352
They were laying guide ropes,

144
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:30,492
inching deeper into the flooded tunnels

145
00:04:30,506 --> 00:04:30,776
They surfaced in a dark chamber...

146
00:04:33,209 --> 00:04:35,809
and saw lights moving on the rocks above

147
00:04:35,575 --> 00:04:35,845
One by one,

148
00:04:36,665 --> 00:04:39,265
figures came down to the water's edge

149
00:04:39,055 --> 00:04:39,325
It was them

150
00:04:40,555 --> 00:04:41,875
All thirteen were alive,

151
00:04:41,875 --> 00:04:44,475
sitting on a muddy ledge above the water

152
00:04:44,267 --> 00:04:44,537
They were thin and weak

153
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,978
But they were smiling

154
00:04:47,708 --> 00:04:47,978
'How many of you?' one diver asked

155
00:04:51,065 --> 00:04:52,893
'Thirteen,' came the answer

156
00:04:52,893 --> 00:04:54,013
'Brilliant.'

157
00:04:54,010 --> 00:04:54,280
The divers promised that many more people were

158
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,159
coming to help

159
00:04:57,889 --> 00:04:58,159
The video of that moment was watched around the

160
00:05:00,539 --> 00:05:01,651
world

161
00:05:01,231 --> 00:05:01,651
Back home,

162
00:05:02,311 --> 00:05:03,995
families cried with joy

163
00:05:03,995 --> 00:05:06,595
But the hardest part was still to come

164
00:05:10,167 --> 00:05:12,747
Because finding them was only the beginning

165
00:05:12,747 --> 00:05:14,427
How do you get thirteen people out of a

166
00:05:14,427 --> 00:05:15,867
flooded mountain?

167
00:05:15,708 --> 00:05:15,978
The next day,

168
00:05:16,784 --> 00:05:18,478
Thai Navy divers brought food,

169
00:05:18,478 --> 00:05:20,238
medicine and blankets

170
00:05:20,357 --> 00:05:20,627
But getting out meant diving through long

171
00:05:22,567 --> 00:05:23,607
flooded tunnels,

172
00:05:23,607 --> 00:05:25,887
some so narrow that divers had to squeeze

173
00:05:25,887 --> 00:05:26,789
through

174
00:05:26,519 --> 00:05:26,789
Four Thai Navy divers,

175
00:05:28,169 --> 00:05:29,449
including a doctor,

176
00:05:29,449 --> 00:05:31,489
stayed with the boys in the dark until the

177
00:05:31,489 --> 00:05:32,743
very end

178
00:05:32,473 --> 00:05:32,743
And here's the problem:

179
00:05:33,843 --> 00:05:36,157
the boys had never been cave diving

180
00:05:36,157 --> 00:05:38,413
Some of them couldn't even swim

181
00:05:38,143 --> 00:05:38,413
The boys wrote letters to their families,

182
00:05:40,593 --> 00:05:42,620
telling them not to worry

183
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:42,620
Meanwhile,

184
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,560
more rain was coming,

185
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,948
enough to flood the cave for months

186
00:05:46,678 --> 00:05:46,948
Some experts suggested waiting months for the

187
00:05:49,648 --> 00:05:51,257
water to go down

188
00:05:50,987 --> 00:05:51,257
But there was another danger

189
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:55,659
The oxygen in their chamber was running low

190
00:05:55,606 --> 00:05:56,026
It had fallen to about fifteen percent

191
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,600
Normal air has twenty-one

192
00:06:04,567 --> 00:06:05,327
To get them out,

193
00:06:05,327 --> 00:06:06,887
divers worked day and night,

194
00:06:06,887 --> 00:06:09,404
placing air tanks along the route

195
00:06:09,134 --> 00:06:09,404
Hundreds of tanks were needed,

196
00:06:11,064 --> 00:06:13,105
carried in one by one

197
00:06:12,835 --> 00:06:13,105
On July 6th,

198
00:06:14,085 --> 00:06:17,045
a former Thai Navy diver named Saman Kunan was

199
00:06:17,045 --> 00:06:19,645
delivering tanks deep inside the cave

200
00:06:20,056 --> 00:06:20,326
He was thirty-eight years old,

201
00:06:21,907 --> 00:06:24,507
and had left the Navy years before

202
00:06:24,246 --> 00:06:24,516
On the way back,

203
00:06:25,376 --> 00:06:26,764
he ran out of air

204
00:06:26,764 --> 00:06:28,681
And he lost his life

205
00:06:28,411 --> 00:06:28,681
His dive partner tried to save him,

206
00:06:30,661 --> 00:06:32,507
but it was too late

207
00:06:32,237 --> 00:06:32,507
He had volunteered to help

208
00:06:34,341 --> 00:06:36,718
And he became a national hero

209
00:06:36,448 --> 00:06:36,718
Across Thailand,

210
00:06:37,778 --> 00:06:38,538
people mourned,

211
00:06:38,538 --> 00:06:41,138
and his story was told around the world

212
00:06:40,956 --> 00:06:41,226
His loss showed just how deadly this rescue

213
00:06:43,726 --> 00:06:44,866
could be

214
00:06:44,446 --> 00:06:44,866
And it raised a terrifying question:

215
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:49,006
if an expert diver could die in there,

216
00:06:49,006 --> 00:06:51,606
how could thirteen boys get out?

217
00:06:55,367 --> 00:06:57,447
The plan they came up with sounded almost

218
00:06:57,447 --> 00:06:58,567
impossible

219
00:06:58,601 --> 00:06:58,831
Dozens of the world's best cave divers had come

220
00:07:01,531 --> 00:07:02,614
together

221
00:07:02,344 --> 00:07:02,614
Each boy would wear a full-face mask,

222
00:07:04,554 --> 00:07:07,154
and be carried out by an expert diver

223
00:07:07,086 --> 00:07:07,356
They practiced first in a swimming pool,

224
00:07:09,376 --> 00:07:11,976
with local children of the same size

225
00:07:11,778 --> 00:07:12,048
And to keep the boys calm underwater,

226
00:07:13,988 --> 00:07:16,948
an Australian doctor who was also a cave diver

227
00:07:16,948 --> 00:07:19,548
gave each boy medicine to make him sleep

228
00:07:19,466 --> 00:07:19,736
It was risky

229
00:07:21,126 --> 00:07:23,726
But the doctors believed it was the only way

230
00:07:23,815 --> 00:07:24,085
Then the divers would guide them,

231
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:26,745
one by one,

232
00:07:26,745 --> 00:07:27,945
through hours of dark,

233
00:07:27,945 --> 00:07:29,385
flooded passages

234
00:07:29,614 --> 00:07:29,884
In the dry sections,

235
00:07:31,024 --> 00:07:33,224
rescuers carried the boys on stretchers,

236
00:07:33,224 --> 00:07:35,812
and hauled them over rocks with ropes

237
00:07:35,542 --> 00:07:35,812
Would it work?

238
00:07:37,246 --> 00:07:38,686
Nobody knew

239
00:07:38,561 --> 00:07:38,981
Every boy's life depended on the diver holding

240
00:07:41,681 --> 00:07:42,801
him

241
00:07:46,267 --> 00:07:47,454
July 8th

242
00:07:47,454 --> 00:07:49,214
The rescue begins

243
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:49,385
Journalists were moved away from the cave,

244
00:07:51,565 --> 00:07:53,628
and the area was cleared

245
00:07:53,358 --> 00:07:53,628
Thirteen foreign divers and five Thai Navy

246
00:07:56,168 --> 00:07:57,622
divers went in

247
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:57,622
Each boy was paired with a diver,

248
00:07:59,402 --> 00:08:02,002
who held him close and followed the guide rope

249
00:08:02,215 --> 00:08:02,485
The journey out took hours

250
00:08:04,338 --> 00:08:06,418
For every single boy

251
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:08,780
Rescuers waited at points along the route to

252
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,226
help carry them

253
00:08:09,956 --> 00:08:10,226
That evening,

254
00:08:10,966 --> 00:08:12,917
the first four boys came out

255
00:08:12,917 --> 00:08:14,037
Alive

256
00:08:14,511 --> 00:08:15,311
Waiting outside,

257
00:08:15,311 --> 00:08:17,511
families still didn't know which boys had made

258
00:08:17,511 --> 00:08:18,296
it

259
00:08:18,026 --> 00:08:18,296
The boys were rushed to hospital by helicopter

260
00:08:20,956 --> 00:08:22,396
and ambulance

261
00:08:22,146 --> 00:08:22,566
And the doctors' verdict?

262
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:26,980
They were in good condition

263
00:08:30,467 --> 00:08:31,107
The next day,

264
00:08:31,107 --> 00:08:32,027
July 9th,

265
00:08:32,027 --> 00:08:34,416
four more boys were carried out

266
00:08:34,146 --> 00:08:34,416
It went faster this time

267
00:08:36,219 --> 00:08:38,530
The team was getting better at it

268
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:38,530
On July 10th,

269
00:08:39,470 --> 00:08:42,070
the last four boys and their coach followed

270
00:08:41,956 --> 00:08:42,226
The four Navy divers who had stayed with the

271
00:08:44,366 --> 00:08:46,859
boys were the very last to leave

272
00:08:46,589 --> 00:08:46,859
And then,

273
00:08:47,439 --> 00:08:49,479
just after the last divers came out,

274
00:08:49,479 --> 00:08:51,342
a main pump failed...

275
00:08:51,342 --> 00:08:53,796
and the water began to rise again

276
00:08:53,526 --> 00:08:53,796
Some rescuers were still deep inside,

277
00:08:55,896 --> 00:08:57,829
and had to rush out

278
00:08:57,559 --> 00:08:57,829
But after eighteen days,

279
00:08:59,129 --> 00:09:00,999
all thirteen were safe

280
00:09:00,729 --> 00:09:00,999
The Thai Navy wrote online:

281
00:09:02,619 --> 00:09:04,539
We are not sure if this is a miracle,

282
00:09:04,539 --> 00:09:05,259
a science,

283
00:09:05,259 --> 00:09:06,442
or what

284
00:09:06,172 --> 00:09:06,442
And the whole world celebrated

285
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:08,960
Football teams and stars around the world sent

286
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,140
messages,

287
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:14,740
and invited the boys to big matches

288
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:21,406
So what happened to the boys after the cave?

289
00:09:21,406 --> 00:09:23,246
They spent about a week in hospital,

290
00:09:23,246 --> 00:09:25,006
and recovered well

291
00:09:24,823 --> 00:09:25,093
At first,

292
00:09:25,673 --> 00:09:27,793
families could only see them through a glass

293
00:09:27,793 --> 00:09:28,233
window,

294
00:09:28,233 --> 00:09:30,171
in case of infection

295
00:09:29,901 --> 00:09:30,171
On average,

296
00:09:30,991 --> 00:09:33,591
each boy had lost about two kilograms

297
00:09:33,508 --> 00:09:33,778
Later,

298
00:09:34,318 --> 00:09:36,438
most of them spent time as novice monks,

299
00:09:36,438 --> 00:09:39,038
to honor the diver who gave his life

300
00:09:38,924 --> 00:09:39,194
They lived at a temple for several days,

301
00:09:41,534 --> 00:09:43,294
praying and meditating

302
00:09:43,299 --> 00:09:43,569
Four of them,

303
00:09:44,269 --> 00:09:45,669
who had no nationality,

304
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:48,069
were later granted Thai citizenship

305
00:09:48,116 --> 00:09:48,386
Books,

306
00:09:48,966 --> 00:09:51,566
documentaries and films told their story

307
00:09:51,677 --> 00:09:51,947
The divers were celebrated as heroes

308
00:09:54,522 --> 00:09:54,792
But many of them said the real heroes were

309
00:09:57,052 --> 00:09:57,692
the boys,

310
00:09:57,692 --> 00:10:00,029
who stayed calm in the dark

311
00:09:59,609 --> 00:10:00,009
Today,

312
00:10:00,529 --> 00:10:02,117
the boys are grown up

313
00:10:02,117 --> 00:10:04,717
And some of them still play football

314
00:10:08,267 --> 00:10:10,722
How many people did it take to save them?

315
00:10:10,722 --> 00:10:12,482
Around ten thousand

316
00:10:12,453 --> 00:10:12,723
That included about ninety divers,

317
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:17,307
from Thailand and around the world

318
00:10:17,037 --> 00:10:17,307
Divers and doctors,

319
00:10:18,687 --> 00:10:20,727
but also cooks who fed the rescuers,

320
00:10:20,727 --> 00:10:23,047
and farmers who let their fields flood with

321
00:10:23,047 --> 00:10:24,434
pumped water

322
00:10:24,164 --> 00:10:24,434
Many of them were volunteers,

323
00:10:26,134 --> 00:10:28,383
who simply showed up to help

324
00:10:28,113 --> 00:10:28,383
It showed what people can do when the whole

325
00:10:30,523 --> 00:10:32,235
world works together

326
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:32,235
Today,

327
00:10:32,815 --> 00:10:35,175
visitors come to the cave to learn about the

328
00:10:35,175 --> 00:10:36,295
rescue

329
00:10:36,053 --> 00:10:36,323
A statue of Saman Kunan stands near the cave,

330
00:10:39,103 --> 00:10:41,703
remembering the hero who didn't come back

331
00:10:41,804 --> 00:10:42,074
And during the rainy season,

332
00:10:43,574 --> 00:10:44,734
the cave is closed,

333
00:10:44,734 --> 00:10:46,927
just as the old sign warned

334
00:10:46,657 --> 00:10:46,927
It's a reminder to respect nature,

335
00:10:48,947 --> 00:10:51,188
and to never give up hope

336
00:10:50,918 --> 00:10:51,188
Because in the end,

337
00:10:52,088 --> 00:10:54,168
thirteen lives were saved

338
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,563
Twelve boys

339
00:10:56,563 --> 00:10:57,718
One coach

340
00:10:57,718 --> 00:10:59,613
Eighteen days in the dark

341
00:10:59,563 --> 00:10:59,613
Thousands of helpers,

342
00:11:00,753 --> 00:11:03,090
and one hero who never came home

343
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:03,090
What would you have done,

344
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:05,992
trapped in that cave?

345
00:11:05,942 --> 00:11:05,992
Tell me in the comments

346
00:11:07,628 --> 00:11:07,678
And subscribe,

347
00:11:08,578 --> 00:11:11,178
so you don't miss the next story
